body:
**What version of ESLint are you using?**
2.2.0

**What configuration and parser (Espree, Babel-ESLint, etc.) are you using?**
babel-eslint

**What did you do? Please include the actual source code causing the issue.**
.eslintrc:

```
{
  "parser": "babel-eslint",

  "env": {
    "node": true,
    "es6": true
  }
}
```

Take the built eslint npm artifacts and put them in one directory -- let's call that $eslint_parent.

Take the built babel-eslint npm artifacts and put them in another directory -- let's call that $babel_eslint_parent.

Create a symlink farm of node modules, call that $symlink_farm:

```
$symlink_farm
 |- eslint -> $eslint_parent/eslint
 |- babel-eslint -> $babel_eslint_parent/babel-eslint
 |- resolve -> ... # some other root
 |- ...  # other modules
```

Run this command:

```
export NODE_PATH=$symlink_farm
node $symlink_farm/eslint/bin/eslint.js  --no-ignore src/ 
```

**What did you expect to happen?**
No errors.

**What actually happened? Please include the actual, raw output from ESLint.**

```
Error: Cannot find module 'babel-eslint' from '$eslint_parent'
    at Function.module.exports [as sync] ($resolve_parent/resolve/lib/sync.js:33:11)
    at Object.load ($eslint_parent/eslint/lib/config/config-file.js:459:43)
    ...
```

Relevant part of eslint's config-file.js at https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/v2.2.0/lib/config/config-file.js#L451 

```
            config.parser = resolveModule.sync(config.parser, {
                basedir: getLookupPath(path.dirname(path.resolve(filePath)))
            });
```

and getLookupPath:

```
function getLookupPath(configFilePath) {

    // calculates the path of the project including ESLint as dependency
    var projectPath = path.resolve(__dirname, "../../../");
    if (configFilePath && pathIsInside(configFilePath, projectPath)) {
        // be careful of https://github.com/substack/node-resolve/issues/78
        return path.resolve(configFilePath);
    }

    // default to ESLint project path since it's unlikely that plugins will be
    // in this directory
    return projectPath;
}
```

The problem is that __dirname is the fully-resolved $eslint_parent/eslint/lib/config/config-file.js instead of $symlink_farm/eslint/lib/config/config-file.js.  So path.resolve(__dirname, "../../../") means $eslint_parent instead of $symlink_farm, and $eslint_parent/babel-eslint does not exist.

Rather than reimplementing node's module path lookup mechanism, using it directly would avoid the issue.  This change for example works for me:

```
config.parser = resolveParser(config.parser, filePath);
...
function resolveParser(parser, filePath) {
  try {
    return require.resolve(parser);
  } catch (e) {
    try {
      return require.resolve('eslint-plugin-', parser);
    } catch (e) {
      return resolveModule.sync(parser, {
          basedir: getLookupPath(path.dirname(path.resolve(filePath)))
      });
    }
  }
}
```
